# SRG-APP-000166-AU-002490  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to enforce password complexity
# by requiring that at least one uppercase character be used.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000166-AU-002490
group:           V-206469
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      documented
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    Splunk's native authentication can require a minimum number of uppercase
                 characters in every password it accepts.

governs:         authentication.conf - How users sign in, and the password rules applied to local accounts.

check:           authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase min 1
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/authentication.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where authType is LDAP or SAML, password complexity for federated accounts
                 is enforced by the directory service or identity provider; [splunk_auth]
                 governs the remaining native accounts
external:        Operating system account passwords on the host

citation:        SPLK-CL-000340 check text ("If the minPasswordUppercase is missing or is
                 configured to 0, this is a finding") and fix text ("minPasswordUppercase =
                 1"); authentication.conf.spec:450-458 (positive integer, default 0,
                 rejects non-conforming password changes)
finding:         authentication.conf [splunk_auth] minPasswordUppercase is absent or 0, so
                 the application accepts native account passwords with no uppercase
                 character.
